WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.154
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for the child who can read a word, but cannot write it.

2
00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:12.770
Here is the goal. On day ten, your child writes short words they have never practiced, and reads each one back to check it.

3
00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:20.126
That is the goal, not a promise. The check on day ten shows you what changed, and what to do if it is not there yet.

4
00:00:20.926 --> 00:00:24.957
This plan is for a child who can read short words, like sun and hat.

5
00:00:25.407 --> 00:00:27.849
But when it is time to write them, it goes wrong.

6
00:00:28.299 --> 00:00:33.376
A sound is left out. The letters are in the wrong order. Or your child just freezes.

7
00:00:33.826 --> 00:00:40.218
Reading before spelling is the usual order at five and six. It is not a sign that something is wrong.

8
00:00:41.018 --> 00:00:46.612
Here is why. In reading, the letters are on the page. In spelling, nothing is on the page.

9
00:00:47.062 --> 00:00:54.131
Your child has to pull the word apart, keep the sounds in order, and pick a letter for each one. It is reading backwards.

10
00:00:54.931 --> 00:00:58.470
So the whole plan is one move, in four steps. Watch.

11
00:00:58.920 --> 00:00:59.756
Say it. Sun.

12
00:01:00.206 --> 00:01:02.163
Tap it. One box for each sound.

13
00:01:05.737 --> 00:01:07.772
Write it. One letter in each box.

14
00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:13.357
Then read it back. Does it say sun?

15
00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.768
The word is sun.

16
00:01:18.668 --> 00:01:22.285
Reading it back is how your child checks a word alone, without you.

17
00:01:23.085 --> 00:01:27.590
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

18
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:34.078
Day one is a short check. It shows you where the spelling gets stuck. Day ten shows you what changed.

19
00:01:34.528 --> 00:01:39.785
Every day has a short video like this one, for you. It shows you what to do before you do it.

20
00:01:40.235 --> 00:01:47.804
On three days there is a sound track for your child. Your child writes first. Then the voice gives the answer, word by word.

21
00:01:48.604 --> 00:01:54.857
Now, what to expect. First one sound at a time: the first, the last, then the middle. Then the whole word.

22
00:01:55.307 --> 00:01:58.549
The boxes help at the start. On day eight they are gone.

23
00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:03.634
Some days need a second try. Doing a page twice is not falling behind.

24
00:02:04.084 --> 00:02:07.113
On day ten, the check gives you one of three next steps.

25
00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:14.400
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

26
00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:19.418
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

27
00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:23.016
Do the first job together. That takes about two minutes.

28
00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:27.535
Then your child carries on with the page, and shows you three things at the end.

29
00:02:27.985 --> 00:02:34.568
Your child spells from pictures, so there is no word to copy. Name the pictures together before you step away.

30
00:02:35.018 --> 00:02:38.274
You need the printed pages, a pencil, and some crayons.

31
00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:43.812
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
